{
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "id": "zone-mines",
  "category": "environment",
  "status": "provisional",
  "comment": "THE CRYSTAL MINES: the cold blue of a lamp in a mine — rock that goes up into the dark, the roof with its teeth, timber that holds the galleries up and crystals that shine. What makes the zone that zone: the three seamless strips of its backdrop, tall enough for the camera of every room of it; the ground its rooms are built of; the pieces that stand, lie and hang in them; the spikes of its ditches; and the light in its colour. Painted by the generator in tools/art (npm run art:build), not by a person: provisional until an artist reviews or replaces it.",
  "tags": [
    "mines",
    "generated"
  ],
  "atlasMode": "shared",
